WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
Add a few drops of
phenolphthalein to an acid.

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.910
It stays colourless.

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.310
Run in alkali from a
burette, drop by drop.

4
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.750
Still colourless.

5
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.950
Then, near the very end,
the whole flask turns pink.

6
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.370
How does a colourless dye suddenly
turn pink at the end of a titration?

7
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.810
In this mission, you'll find
out what an indicator really is,

8
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.390
and where its colour change happens.

9
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.550
You'll see why universal indicator
is no use in a titration,

10
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.550
and choose the right indicator
for each kind of titration.

11
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:37.490
Your mission: explain why phenolphthalein
turns pink at the end of a titration.
